---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="About" description="Senior Product Designer. Cognitive science and biochemistry before design.">
  <header class="hero shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="display hero__title">
      I want to know what the system actually does before I decide what it should look like.
    </h1>
  </header>

  <div class="prose shell">
    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>
      I came to design sideways. Four and a half years in a biochemistry lab, then cognitive
      science with an HCI specialization at UC San Diego, then a Master of Engineering in
      Product Design &amp; Development Management at Northwestern.
    </p>
    <p>
      The lab is the part that still shows up in how I work. Bench science teaches you that the
      hard part of a problem is usually the measurement, not the answer — and that a result you
      cannot explain is not a result yet. That turns out to describe fraud tooling almost exactly.
    </p>

    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <p>
      I spend longer than most designers on what the system actually does before deciding what it
      should look like. In risk products the interface is downstream of a model, a policy, and a
      regulator, and none of those are negotiable from Figma. Understanding them first is what
      makes the design work survive contact with engineering.
    </p>
    <p>
      Most of the last several years has been fraud and risk at Kount, an Equifax company —
      payments fraud, chargebacks, account protection, and authorized payment protection, all on
      the Kount 360 platform, whose original information architecture I designed. I work closely
      with data science, because in these products the interesting decisions live in the seam
      between what a model produces and what a person is willing to defend.
    </p>
    <p>
      I also speak Spanish, which has repeatedly put me in stakeholder conversations I would
      otherwise have received secondhand.
    </p>

    <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
    <p>
      Seattle, working remotely. Outside of work: hiking, swimming, beach volleyball, and soccer
      when the weather cooperates, and guitar, new breweries, and the classics when it doesn't.
      This site is built with Astro and deployed from GitHub — notes on how and why are coming.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding-block: var(--space-3xl) var(--space-2xl); }
  .hero__title { font-size: var(--type-h1); margin-block-start: var(--space-lg); max-width: 32ch; }
  .prose { padding-block-end: var(--space-3xl); }
</style>
